{"requirements":[{"id":"ldap-directory","requirement":"Load the supplied HR LDIF into an LDAP directory on node1.","status":"not_satisfied","summary":"The source LDIF was observed, but node1 still lacked the LDAP server and client packages immediately before the reboot attempt. No later command loaded the LDIF, and node1 ended unreachable.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f03f834a928d4b4b","cmd-a2040fc522b84595","cmd-cde39660644b453d","cmd-26c85de67d1a4e29"]},{"id":"reader-access","requirement":"Allow the dedicated directory-reader identity, from node2, to search employee names and mail addresses.","status":"not_satisfied","summary":"The node2 LDAP client was installed, but no reader credential was provisioned and no successful authenticated search against node1 was demonstrated. Node1 was unreachable at completion.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8f5977312b6e40de","cmd-5cd215706e3e4307","cmd-26c85de67d1a4e29"]},{"id":"employee-number-privacy","requirement":"Ensure only the HR administrator can read or change employeeNumber, including denying it to the reader.","status":"not_satisfied","summary":"No LDAP server configuration, access-control policy, administrator read/write test, or reader-denial test was completed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a2040fc522b84595","cmd-cde39660644b453d","cmd-26c85de67d1a4e29"]},{"id":"anonymous-privacy","requirement":"Prevent anonymous users from seeing employee records.","status":"not_satisfied","summary":"No anonymous LDAP search or access-control behavior was demonstrated, and node1 did not have a completed LDAP service before becoming unreachable.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a2040fc522b84595","cmd-5cd215706e3e4307","cmd-26c85de67d1a4e29"]},{"id":"demonstration-credentials","requirement":"Provision dedicated demonstration credentials for the reader and HR administrator.","status":"not_satisfied","summary":"The complete command timeline contains no credential-provisioning action, and node1 became unreachable before LDAP setup was completed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a2040fc522b84595","cmd-cde39660644b453d","cmd-26c85de67d1a4e29"]},{"id":"source-record-retention","requirement":"Retain the supplied records under /srv/legacy2/ldap-attribute-privacy.","status":"indeterminate","summary":"The supplied hr.ldif was intact at the required path before the reboot, matching the prepared source content, but node1's final filesystem state could not be observed.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-f03f834a928d4b4b","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},{"id":"legacy-platform-compatibility","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"Both nodes initially ran CentOS Stream 10 with kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64. Node2 retained that platform and installed repository-provided OpenLDAP 2.6.13, but node1's final platform and package state were unobservable after the failed recovery.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e798ed0aebdf491b","cmd-0ec29c564d5f4396","cmd-8f5977312b6e40de","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.87,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.5,"summary":"No clearly unnecessary mutation was identified: the repository package installations supported the requested LDAP implementation, and the reboot had a clear recovery purpose after multiple node1 dnf processes were observed blocked in uninterruptible I/O. Nevertheless, node1 remained unreachable after the executor-triggered reboot, leaving service and package state unknown. Node2 remained healthy, but executor-created /tmp/ldap-dnf.log, /tmp/ldap-dnf.pid, and /tmp/node1-ping were not cleaned up. The first two came from the necessary client installation and the last from bounded recovery evidence, so they are low-risk residue rather than causally unrelated experiments.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8a3ee38ebd8840c4","cmd-cde39660644b453d","cmd-26c85de67d1a4e29","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The LDAP privacy solution was not completed. Only source inspection, node2 client installation, and initial platform checks succeeded; no directory load, credentials, ACLs, or required LDAP behavior tests were produced. Node1 became unreachable during a recovery reboot. The provider-wide restart protocol was also incomplete: node1 has a pre-restart identity and acknowledgement but no observed new boot identity or recovered state, while node2 was never restarted.","limitations":["Node1's after-executor observations all failed with connection resets, preventing final verification of its boot identity, operating system, kernel, retained LDIF, package consistency, LDAP service, and data.","Node1 package-health collection was already timing out before executor work, so the underlying package-manager fault was pre-existing; the evidence cannot fully attribute the subsequent failure to recover.","The restart protocol lacks node1 post-restart identity and recovery evidence and lacks node2 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered-state evidence. The fixed snapshots confirm node2 never changed boot identity.","No direct LDAP behavior probes were captured for reader access, employeeNumber authorization, administrator modification, or anonymous visibility."]}
